WEBVTT

00:01.590 --> 00:05.340
Fly, champions,
toward the grand finale of Oban.

00:05.510 --> 00:07.760
Toward the Ultimate Prize!

00:07.930 --> 00:09.720
<i>Rick Thunderbolt's
terrible accident</i>

00:09.890 --> 00:12.260
<i>in the first race was
a shock for everyone.</i>

00:13.220 --> 00:16.390
<i>Now we had no one to pilot
the Arrow 2, except for me,</i>

00:16.560 --> 00:17.850
<i>Molly, the team's black sheep.</i>

00:20.900 --> 00:24.190
<i>It was a chance to show Don Wei,
our manager, otherwise known</i>

00:24.360 --> 00:26.320
<i>as my dad, what I was made of.</i>

00:34.950 --> 00:35.950
It was a great race.

00:36.620 --> 00:40.120
<i>Don Wei doesn't know
that I'm really his daughter Eva.</i>

00:41.710 --> 00:44.960
<i>But maybe he'll love me
as the pilot Molly.</i>

02:23.310 --> 02:24.520
Rise and shine!

02:24.850 --> 02:26.650
We've got a lot to do today!

02:28.860 --> 02:30.690
Sorry, Mom.
I didn't hear the alarm.

02:31.820 --> 02:32.860
Hey, wait a second!

02:33.990 --> 02:35.280
Good morning, Koji.

02:35.610 --> 02:37.160
How's my Arrow doing today?

02:37.370 --> 02:39.280
Well, uh, it's good.

02:39.580 --> 02:42.540
Stan is just finishing
one last little upgrade.

02:42.700 --> 02:43.620
Terrific.

02:43.790 --> 02:45.750
I know it's going to be
a great day.

02:50.090 --> 02:51.130
There she is.

02:51.920 --> 02:53.920
Here's looking at you, kid.

02:54.800 --> 02:55.800
Huh? What?

02:58.010 --> 03:01.260
Stan, what have you done
with my rocket seat?

03:01.810 --> 03:04.060
You know the standard seat's
too big for me.

03:04.230 --> 03:06.310
Yeah. But it's perfect for me.

03:11.270 --> 03:12.730
Rick?

03:12.900 --> 03:14.400
Uh, you're back?

03:15.200 --> 03:16.740
Yeah, I'm back.

03:16.860 --> 03:18.450
Those Alwas doctors
have technologies

03:18.620 --> 03:20.990
that far surpass
the ones we have on Earth.

03:21.160 --> 03:23.160
So, I heard
you kept my seat warm.

03:23.330 --> 03:24.500
It was nothing.

03:24.790 --> 03:25.960
Really.

03:29.250 --> 03:30.460
Thanks, little mouse.

03:31.130 --> 03:32.920
You'll have to tell me all about it.

03:33.090 --> 03:34.840
Modesty's for losers.

03:36.550 --> 03:38.930
Well, actually...

03:39.180 --> 03:40.890
Rick! Haha!

03:41.510 --> 03:42.600
Rick, you're back!

03:42.760 --> 03:44.060
That's so cool.

03:44.730 --> 03:46.980
Boy, we really missed you
around here.

03:47.140 --> 03:49.900
Easy, Jordan!
No hugging. Doctor's orders.

03:50.360 --> 03:51.230
But Rick!

03:51.400 --> 03:54.820
I guess I'll let you two catch up.
I need to find someone.

04:09.710 --> 04:10.880
We're all set, Koji.

04:17.340 --> 04:18.430
Hey, you!

04:21.050 --> 04:23.350
Why didn't you tell me
Rick was coming back?

04:23.510 --> 04:25.520
This is not the moment,
young lady.

04:27.100 --> 04:28.480
It's never the moment, is it?

04:31.100 --> 04:32.110
Hey!

04:34.860 --> 04:35.980
All right now, Rick.

04:36.360 --> 04:38.360
Let's do a quick check
of the new reactors.

04:38.530 --> 04:39.530
Sure. I'm ready.

04:40.910 --> 04:42.160
Jordan's ready, too!

04:42.320 --> 04:44.490
Start out easy.
Nothing fancy.

04:54.540 --> 04:58.010
Thrusters are at 80%,
balanced at 100%.

04:58.170 --> 05:00.430
-All is normal.
-That's excellent.

05:00.590 --> 05:02.340
Go ahead, Rick.
Let her rip.

05:02.680 --> 05:05.470
You got it.
I have a need for speed.

05:14.650 --> 05:17.190
Now we're talking.
The star is back!

05:20.610 --> 05:21.660
What?

05:22.660 --> 05:24.120
What's happening to me?

05:32.540 --> 05:33.500
<i>What's he doing?</i>

05:33.670 --> 05:36.040
<i>Why doesn't he straighten up?
He'll crash.</i>

05:41.130 --> 05:43.130
Rick! What's going on?

05:43.550 --> 05:45.300
Rick! ls everything OK?

06:02.950 --> 06:04.990
Oh, yeah! That was great!

06:05.160 --> 06:07.490
I'm calling it
the Thunderbolt Zigzag.

06:09.370 --> 06:12.500
Everything's fine.
I was just hotdogging a bit.

06:15.500 --> 06:16.920
<i>That's not like Rick.</i>

06:17.090 --> 06:19.090
<i>He'd never take that kind of risk.</i>

06:32.560 --> 06:34.560
Hey, great ride, Rick!

06:35.810 --> 06:37.520
Hey, thanks a lot, you guys.

06:39.570 --> 06:40.690
It's good to be back.

06:41.610 --> 06:43.150
I'm going up to rest.

06:45.410 --> 06:46.410
Rick. Wait up.

06:50.540 --> 06:53.000
Man, Rick's awesome.

06:54.160 --> 06:57.040
It's sure great to have a real pro
at the controls again.

07:03.670 --> 07:05.630
Molly, come on.
You know what I mean.

07:05.840 --> 07:07.760
I mean, you're good and all,
but this is Rick.

07:08.010 --> 07:09.800
Rick? You're here?

07:28.410 --> 07:30.240
What's happening to me?

07:31.080 --> 07:33.830
Stop shaking!

07:36.330 --> 07:37.250
Stop!

07:42.090 --> 07:43.380
Rick?

07:43.880 --> 07:45.340
Who said you could just walk in here?

07:45.760 --> 07:47.470
I need a little rest.

07:47.630 --> 07:48.970
Can't you understand that?

07:49.140 --> 07:50.350
Rick, I'm really sorry.

07:50.510 --> 07:52.180
But I heard a noise,
and I just wanted to...

07:52.470 --> 07:53.770
There was no noise.

07:54.020 --> 07:55.060
You're disturbing me.

07:55.230 --> 07:56.980
I must have been mistaken.

08:20.710 --> 08:23.590
I'll be fine.
<i>I</i> just need some rest.

08:32.930 --> 08:33.760
Jordan?

08:33.930 --> 08:36.100
-Do you have a minute?
-What's up?

08:36.560 --> 08:38.230
I'm kind of worried about Rick.

08:38.480 --> 08:40.730
Did you notice anything odd
when you were riding with him?

08:42.360 --> 08:44.570
At first I was worried.

08:45.610 --> 08:47.820
But then I thought,
well, hey this is Rick.

08:47.940 --> 08:49.320
Come on, Molly, admit it.

08:49.490 --> 08:51.660
Rick gave us
a great flying lesson today.

08:52.410 --> 08:54.370
-OK, forget it.
-Coming through.

08:56.330 --> 08:57.080
Hey, Koji?

08:58.580 --> 08:59.620
Do you think it's normal

09:00.210 --> 09:01.670
that Rick would take chances

09:02.130 --> 09:03.790
like he did today?

09:04.920 --> 09:08.920
Molly, you wouldn't be
jealous of Rick, would you?

09:09.300 --> 09:11.340
That's not what I mean.
I'm worried that...

09:11.510 --> 09:13.180
Molly, let Koji work.

09:13.300 --> 09:15.140
There's little time
before the next race.

09:15.760 --> 09:17.100
All you ever care about is the race.

09:18.060 --> 09:19.520
That's right.

09:21.230 --> 09:23.650
<i>Nobody listens,
so why do I care?</i>

09:54.550 --> 09:57.390
Why look,
it's my good friend Molly.

09:57.600 --> 10:00.310
Satis, you always show up
at the wrong time.

10:00.480 --> 10:03.310
It's really a question
of perspective, isn't it?

10:04.980 --> 10:05.900
Well?

10:06.820 --> 10:08.650
The race is about to start.

10:08.860 --> 10:11.610
You should be getting ready.
Your friends need you.

10:11.820 --> 10:13.910
-They don't need me anymore.
-What's that?

10:14.490 --> 10:16.200
Nobody cares. Trust me.

10:16.370 --> 10:18.330
When they're finished with you,
it's poof, like...

10:18.790 --> 10:20.620
...like you never existed.

10:21.200 --> 10:24.210
Such dark thoughts
for a girl your age, Molly.

10:24.370 --> 10:27.090
These are normal thoughts
for a girl my age. I should know.

10:29.630 --> 10:30.460
We need to talk.

10:34.260 --> 10:36.970
<i>For the third round
of presentation,</i>

10:37.140 --> 10:40.010
I call forth the Earth team!

10:44.310 --> 10:46.310
The dream team is back!

10:46.480 --> 10:47.980
Hah! By popular demand!

10:52.940 --> 10:56.870
And representing
the Mong people, Ceres!

11:05.370 --> 11:06.960
How could a thing like that fly?

11:07.330 --> 11:09.840
Well, normally it shouldn't.

11:10.250 --> 11:13.760
But it uses some unknown form
of planetary magnetism.

11:13.920 --> 11:14.720
I'd stay alert, boys.

11:24.060 --> 11:25.270
Jordan.

11:25.600 --> 11:27.650
Don't let the stick man scare you.

11:27.850 --> 11:28.980
I'm all right, Rick.

11:52.460 --> 11:56.010
Humans!
Your hour ofjudgement has come!

11:59.930 --> 12:02.180
Something to shake you up a bit.

12:12.070 --> 12:12.900
What was that?

12:18.150 --> 12:19.780
Jordan!
See if you can hold him off!

12:20.110 --> 12:21.200
Watch me!

12:21.910 --> 12:23.660
Take this, stick man!

12:28.960 --> 12:31.380
Your attacks are pitiful!

12:51.600 --> 12:53.820
Go, Rick!
Just like on the test track!

12:54.110 --> 12:55.780
The Thunderbolt Zigzag!

12:57.820 --> 12:58.530
Not now!

13:11.120 --> 13:14.130
<i>You must forgive your friends
for not seeing the real you.</i>

13:14.670 --> 13:18.260
If not, then you're simply
putting a price on friendship.

13:18.380 --> 13:21.260
-Isn't that true?
-We'll chat later. I gotta go!

13:25.010 --> 13:27.970
Why continue this conversation
when you already understand?

13:31.020 --> 13:33.100
Rick, would you stop
playing around with this guy?

13:33.770 --> 13:36.150
-He's dangerous!
-He can't hear you, sir.

13:36.570 --> 13:37.820
He's TKO'd.

13:37.980 --> 13:39.740
His nervous system
is completely shot.

13:39.900 --> 13:41.240
Don't be ridiculous!

13:41.490 --> 13:43.490
He was in perfect shape
this morning.

13:54.130 --> 13:56.920
How can you imagine,
even for a second,

13:57.090 --> 13:59.760
that you are worthy
of the Ultimate Prize?

14:00.340 --> 14:02.760
Humans. Crogs. Nourasians.

14:02.930 --> 14:04.840
They are all the same.

14:05.010 --> 14:07.350
A few thousand years
of existence,

14:07.560 --> 14:10.350
and you think you are important.

14:11.730 --> 14:12.890
Rick, what's going on?

14:16.650 --> 14:18.610
Everything is fine.

14:19.190 --> 14:22.450
I just need to rest a bit.

14:29.950 --> 14:32.370
Rick.
It's worse than I thought.

14:33.830 --> 14:34.790
OK.

14:39.130 --> 14:40.670
Here goes nothing!

14:42.130 --> 14:42.800
NOW!

14:50.560 --> 14:51.640
Molly!

14:54.690 --> 14:55.810
I'm coming, Rick!

15:05.780 --> 15:06.820
Rick?

15:08.200 --> 15:10.030
He must have been knocked out.

15:10.830 --> 15:11.990
Not good!

15:17.880 --> 15:20.500
Little mouse.
What are you doing here?

15:20.710 --> 15:22.670
I'll take the controls.
Can you work the pedals?

15:24.420 --> 15:25.590
I think so.

15:27.760 --> 15:29.050
That's intriguing.

15:29.220 --> 15:31.060
I sense a new spirit.

15:35.060 --> 15:36.480
Now I've got ya!

15:39.940 --> 15:42.190
All resistance is futile.

15:42.440 --> 15:46.490
The Mong people are the last
of the ancient people of the Galaxy.

15:46.650 --> 15:48.990
And I am the last of the Mongs.

15:49.660 --> 15:52.660
You are not even
worthy of facing me.

15:53.040 --> 15:54.040
Then get lost!

15:55.080 --> 15:58.420
I see that you still
do not understand.

15:58.620 --> 16:00.380
In my great mercy,

16:00.540 --> 16:03.460
I shall immediately
put an end to your suffering

16:03.670 --> 16:06.920
and offer you
the most beautiful of gifts.

16:07.180 --> 16:10.220
Let me show you
the world of the Mongs.

17:20.160 --> 17:21.870
Molly, what happened?

17:23.670 --> 17:24.420
Little mouse.

17:25.630 --> 17:26.960
Wake up, Molly.

17:27.380 --> 17:28.300
Wake up.

17:30.340 --> 17:31.970
Wake up!

17:39.730 --> 17:40.770
No!

18:21.810 --> 18:24.770
It was nice of you
to drop in, little mouse.

18:26.110 --> 18:28.610
I've always wanted a co-pilot.

18:28.770 --> 18:30.440
Any time, Rick.

18:32.190 --> 18:33.030
Rick?

18:46.630 --> 18:47.750
We're with you, Rick.

19:07.100 --> 19:09.110
You have
a strong constitution, Rick.

19:09.270 --> 19:10.730
You'll pull through.

19:11.570 --> 19:13.280
But your racing days are over.

19:13.440 --> 19:15.030
What? No way!

19:18.490 --> 19:21.660
Your accident against Grooor
has caused unusual side effects

19:21.830 --> 19:23.700
on your nervous system.

19:24.290 --> 19:27.880
You lose control of your muscles
in moments of violent stress.

19:28.580 --> 19:30.090
Well, then,
you've got to heal him!

19:30.460 --> 19:32.250
Even with our level of technology,

19:32.380 --> 19:35.590
there are some illnesses
that we cannot conquer.

19:37.640 --> 19:40.300
To stay alive, he must never
get into a star-racer again.

19:40.470 --> 19:41.180
Even

19:41.430 --> 19:42.770
That's impossible!

19:43.810 --> 19:46.690
-I can't be sick.
-Rick, stop it!

19:47.480 --> 19:49.020
Don't you understand?

19:49.560 --> 19:51.270
Racing is my whole life!

19:58.740 --> 20:00.700
-Rick, it's...
-No!

20:03.370 --> 20:04.750
Just leave me alone.

20:12.590 --> 20:14.920
-Rick, wait!
-Let him go.

20:15.670 --> 20:17.470
He needs time.

20:19.050 --> 20:21.430
We have a lot
to discuss, young lady.

20:21.800 --> 20:24.970
We'll talk tomorrow.
You were very brave today.
